⚠️ Program 13 — File Error Handling and Stream States

📌 Description

This program demonstrates how to detect and handle file and stream errors using C++ stream-state functions.

It checks whether a file can be opened and demonstrates the use of functions such as "eof()", "fail()", and "bad()" to determine the state of a stream.

🔑 Concepts Covered

- ⚠️ File-opening errors
- 🛡️ Stream-state checking
- "is_open()"
- "good()"
- "eof()"
- "fail()"
- "bad()"
- 🚨 Error reporting

📁 File Used

"missing_file.txt"

🧠 Main Concept

Reliable file-operation error handling
